      "message": "Since the most common progression will likely be each state goes from state N to state N+1 until we reach the end, it might be helpful to also include a `test_multistep_next_step` function. It would effectively call `test_multistep_set_state` with the next state. I imagine it would look something like this:\n\n```\nstatic void test_multistep_next_state(struct test_multistep_state state)\n{\n  struct test_multistep_state prev_state \u003d test_multistep_get_status();\n\n  if (prev_state.step \u003c TEST_MULTISTEP_STEP_16) {\n    test_multistep_set_state((struct test_multistep_state){\n      .status \u003d prev_state.status,\n      .step \u003d prev_state.step+1,\n    });\n  } else {\n    __builtin_unreachable();\n  }\n}\n```\n\nI don\u0027t think it\u0027s required for the CL, just thinking out loud.",
